WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.260
You may not like this, but I’m going to say it anyway.

2
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:09.500
I’m somewhat offended by the heirs looking for some type of reparation.

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.180
Suing for a billion dollars.

4
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.140
I think that’s ridiculous.

5
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:17.420
I think it’s not rooted in any substance or logic or common sense.

6
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:23.700
Because slavery was legal back at the time they sold my great-great-great-great-great-grandfather.

7
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:28.540
So therefore, there’s no recourse, because it was the law of the land.

8
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.800
Do I subscribe to and support that?

9
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:31.780
Absolutely not.

10
00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.360
But you can’t sue with that.

11
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:42.200
I think it’s a missed opportunity with my newfound relatives, that they are misguided in their venture.

12
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:50.120
The trajectory of this new relationship should be one of creating a bond,

13
00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:57.740
creating a relationship with Georgetown so that kids like me can go and get educated there.

14
00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:03.740
I think Isaac Hawkins’ relatives who have somewhat worked hard and made it, I think we all . . . we all,

15
00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:06.200
and quote me on this, ought to put some skin in the game with this.

16
00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:11.460
Because it’s about helping that kid who’s less fortunate than the rest of us.

17
00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:15.740
Let’s put together a big pot, create something here.

18
00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:20.920
So that kids who look like me, and out of all 272,

19
00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:25.550
can have an opportunity to get this so-called Ivy League education that emanated from Georgetown University.
